To fix the "infinite recursion" error, you need to update your Supabase Row Level Security (RLS) policies. This error happens because the policy for the `profiles` table was trying to check the `profiles` table to verify the user's role, creating a never-ending loop.

### 1. The Fix: Run this SQL in Supabase
Run this corrected SQL in your **Supabase SQL Editor**. It uses **JWT Metadata**, which is much faster and avoids the recursion loop entirely.

```sql
-- 1. Remove the old recursive policies
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Master Admin Full Access" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Admin Manage Own Volunteers" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Profiles access policy" ON public.profiles;

-- 2. Create the new, safe policy using JWT metadata
-- This checks the 'role' we store in the Auth metadata instead of querying the table again.
CREATE POLICY "Profiles access policy" ON public.profiles
FOR ALL TO authenticated
USING (
  id = auth.uid() -- Everyone can see their own
  OR (auth.jwt() -> 'user_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'MasterAdmin'
  OR (
    (auth.jwt() -> 'user_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'Organisation' 
    AND 
    organisation_id = (auth.jwt() -> 'user_metadata' ->> 'organisation_id')::uuid
  )
);

-- 3. Update Members table policies to be equally efficient
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Master Admin Members Access" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Admin Members Access" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Volunteer Own Submissions" ON public.members;

CREATE POLICY "Members access policy" ON public.members
