The **"Access Denied"** and **"RLS_RECURSION_ERROR"** occur because your security policies are trying to look up a user's role by querying the `profiles` table *while* checking permissions on that same table—creating an infinite loop.

There is a **much cleaner, modern way** to fix this without complex functions: **JWT Metadata**. Instead of asking the database to look up the role every single time, we store the role inside the user's login token (JWT). This makes the check instant and impossible to loop.

### The "Better Way" Fix (Auth Metadata)

1.  **In Supabase SQL Editor**, run this script. It moves the "MasterAdmin" permission out of the table and into the secure login token:

```sql
-- 1. CLEANUP: Remove the looping policies
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins have full access" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users can view own profile" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admins can manage organisations" ON public.organisations;

-- 2. THE FIX: Update Auth Metadata for your admin account
-- This "injects" the role into the token so the DB doesn't have to query itself
UPDATE auth.users 
SET raw_app_metadata_content = jsonb_set(
  COALESCE(raw_app_metadata_content, '{}'::jsonb),
  '{role}',
  '"MasterAdmin"'
)
WHERE email = 'Masteradmin@ssk.com';

-- 3. NEW RECURSION-FREE POLICIES
-- We use auth.jwt() which is already in memory, so NO database lookup happens!
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY "Self View" ON public.profiles 
FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = id);

CREATE POLICY "Admin Power" ON public.profiles 
FOR ALL USING ( (auth.jwt() -> 'app_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'MasterAdmin' );

CREATE POLICY "Admin Org Management" ON public.organisations 
FOR ALL USING ( (auth.jwt() -> 'app_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'MasterAdmin' );

CREATE POLICY "Public Org View" ON public.organisations 
FOR SELECT USING ( true );
```

### Updated Application Code

I've updated the `AuthContext` to recognize roles from the JWT metadata directly. This means even if the database is slow or has issues, the app knows you are an admin immediately upon login.

