To fix the **"Trigger Failure"** once and for all, we need to address the way Postgres handles the data being passed from Supabase Auth. The most common cause of a "crash" is a **type mismatch** (e.g., trying to save an empty string as a UUID) or **permissions**.

### 1. The "Nuclear" SQL Repair
Please run this updated, more robust script in your **Supabase SQL Editor**. It includes an "Error Handler" inside the function to prevent it from crashing even if the data is slightly malformed.

```sql
-- 🛠️ SSK "NUCLEAR" REPAIR SCRIPT
-- This version handles UUID conversion errors and permission locks.

-- 1. Ensure columns exist
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS mobile text;
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS status text DEFAULT 'Active';
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS organisation_id uuid;

-- 2. Robust Trigger Function (With Error Catching)
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user()
RETURNS trigger AS $$
DECLARE
  org_id_raw text;
  org_id_final uuid;
BEGIN
  -- Extract and safely convert UUID
  org_id_raw := new.raw_user_meta_data->>'organisation_id';

  IF org_id_raw IS NOT NULL AND org_id_raw <> '' THEN
    BEGIN
      org_id_final := org_id_raw::uuid;
    EXCEPTION WHEN OTHERS THEN
      org_id_final := NULL; -- Prevent crash if ID is invalid
    END;
  END IF;

  INSERT INTO public.profiles (id, name, email, role, organisation_id, mobile, status)
  VALUES (
    new.id,
    COALESCE(new.raw_user_meta_data->>'name', 'New User'),
    new.email,
    COALESCE(new.raw_user_meta_data->>'role', 'Volunteer'),
    org_id_final,
    new.raw_user_meta_data->>'mobile',
    'Active'
  )
  ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET
    role = EXCLUDED.role,
    organisation_id = EXCLUDED.organisation_id,
    name = EXCLUDED.name,
    mobile = EXCLUDED.mobile;

  RETURN new;
END;
$$ LANGUAGE plpgsql SECURITY DEFINER;

-- 3. Re-attach trigger
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS on_auth_user_created ON auth.users;
CREATE TRIGGER on_auth_user_created
  AFTER INSERT ON auth.users
  FOR EACH ROW EXECUTE FUNCTION public.handle_new_user();

-- 4. Critical: Ensure the trigger bypasses RLS
GRANT ALL ON public.profiles TO service_role;
GRANT ALL ON public.profiles TO postgres;
```

### 2. Frontend Update
I am updating `ManageOrganisations.tsx` to handle the failure even more gracefully. It will now try to verify if the user was created despite the trigger error (Supabase sometimes does this) and perform a manual "healing" step.

