To fix the **"infinite recursion detected in policy"** error, you must clear out the conflicting security rules in your database. This error happens when two or more Row Level Security (RLS) policies are trying to check each other in a loop.

### 1. The "Recursion Killer" SQL Script
Copy and run this in your **Supabase SQL Editor**. It drops all previous conflicting policies and replaces them with a "Flat Logic" system that uses JWT metadata, which is impossible to recurse.

```sql
-- 🔱 SSK RECURSION KILLER & INTEGRITY FIX 🔱

-- 1. Clean up the Members table policies
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Enable select for duplicates" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Volunteers insert own" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Orgs view own members" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "MasterAdmin view all" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Public Aadhaar Check" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Volunteers Insert" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Member Visibility" ON public.members;

-- 2. Create the ultra-stable Flat Policies (No Subqueries = No Recursion)
-- This allows any logged-in user to check Aadhaar numbers (Select) without a loop
CREATE POLICY "members_read_policy" ON public.members 
FOR SELECT TO authenticated 
USING ( true );

-- This allows volunteers to insert members
CREATE POLICY "members_insert_policy" ON public.members 
FOR INSERT TO authenticated 
WITH CHECK ( auth.uid() = volunteer_id );

-- 3. Clean up Profiles table (where recursion often starts)
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Enable all for admins" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Admins Manage Own Volunteers" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users view own" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "MasterAdmin Full Access" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users View Own Profile" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Self View" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Admin Power" ON public.profiles;

-- Use JWT claims for Profile security (Fastest & Safest)
CREATE POLICY "profiles_read_self" ON public.profiles 
FOR SELECT TO authenticated 
USING ( auth.uid() = id OR (auth.jwt() -> 'app_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'MasterAdmin' );

CREATE POLICY "profiles_admin_all" ON public.profiles 
FOR ALL TO authenticated 
USING ( (auth.jwt() -> 'app_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'MasterAdmin' );

-- 4. Final Permissions Wipe
GRANT ALL ON public.members TO authenticated;
GRANT ALL ON public.profiles TO authenticated;
```

### 2. Application Update
I have updated `NewMemberForm.tsx` to detect "recursion" errors specifically and provide the correct fix immediately.

