To fix the **`[object Object]`** errors and resolve the underlying **"Infinite Recursion"** database fault, you need to apply both a SQL fix to your Supabase backend and an update to the application's error-handling logic.

### 1. The Root Cause Fix (Run this in Supabase)
The "Infinite Recursion" happens because your security policies are trying to check permissions by querying the same table they are protecting, creating an endless loop. Copy and run this script in your **Supabase SQL Editor** to replace the looping logic with a stable, high-performance system using JWT claims.

```sql
-- 🔱 SSK "FINAL" SECURITY REPAIR (RECURSION KILLER) 🔱

-- 1. Clean up Members Table
ALTER TABLE public.members DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Public Aadhaar Check" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "members_read_all" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "members_read_policy" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "members_insert_policy" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Member Visibility" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Volunteers Insert" ON public.members;

-- 2. Clean up Profiles Table (Often the source of loops)
ALTER TABLE public.profiles DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "profiles_read_self" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "profiles_admin_all" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Users View Own Profile" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Admins Manage Own Volunteers" ON public.profiles;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "MasterAdmin Full Access" ON public.profiles;

-- 3. Re-enable Security
ALTER TABLE public.members ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- 4. Create Flat Policies (No Subqueries = Zero Recursion)
-- Members: Read access for all authenticated users (needed for duplicate checks)
CREATE POLICY "members_flat_read" ON public.members FOR SELECT 
TO authenticated USING ( true );

-- Members: Insert access linked strictly to Auth ID
CREATE POLICY "members_flat_insert" ON public.members FOR INSERT 
TO authenticated WITH CHECK ( auth.uid() = volunteer_id );

-- Profiles: Self-read only
CREATE POLICY "profiles_flat_read_self" ON public.profiles FOR SELECT 
TO authenticated USING ( auth.uid() = id );

-- Profiles: Admin bypass using JWT metadata (The most stable method)
CREATE POLICY "profiles_flat_admin_all" ON public.profiles FOR ALL 
TO authenticated USING ( (auth.jwt() -> 'app_metadata' ->> 'role') = 'MasterAdmin' );

-- 5. Grant Permissions
GRANT ALL ON public.members TO authenticated;
GRANT ALL ON public.profiles TO authenticated;
```

### 2. Application Update
I have hardened the error extraction logic in `VolunteerDashboard.tsx` and `NewMemberForm.tsx` to ensure that even if the database throws a complex object, the UI will display the text message instead of `[object Object]`.

