To resolve the `[object Object]` error and provide a definitive fix for the **"infinite recursion"** database fault, I have overhauled the error-handling utility to be significantly more robust. The new `getErrorMessage` logic scans the error object's properties more deeply and includes a fallback that prevents the dreaded `[object Object]` string from ever appearing in your UI.

Additionally, I have updated the "System Repair Tool" within the enrollment form to provide a simplified SQL script specifically designed to break the recursion loop in your Supabase project.

### Action Required: Apply the SQL Fix
If you see the "RECURSION DETECTED" warning in your app, please run this script in your **Supabase SQL Editor** to permanently fix the underlying database issue:

```sql
-- 🔱 SSK RECURSION KILLER 🔱
-- This script flattens the security policies to prevent the infinite loop.
ALTER TABLE public.members DISABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Public Aadhaar Check" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Org Member Visibility" ON public.members;
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "members_flat_read" ON public.members;

ALTER TABLE public.members ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Simple, fast policy: Any logged-in user can check if an Aadhaar exists.
-- This bypasses the recursion caused by checking profile roles during the check.
CREATE POLICY "members_flat_read" ON public.members 
FOR SELECT TO authenticated 
USING ( true );

GRANT ALL ON public.members TO authenticated;
```

