To fix the "Active Field Nodes" count and resolve the SQL error you encountered, you need to use an explicit type cast in your SQL query because the `role` column uses a custom type (Enum).

### 1. Fixed SQL Code
Run this in your **Supabase SQL Editor** to enable public access and fix the data consistency:

```sql
-- 1. Enable RLS (Row Level Security) on the tables
ALTER TABLE public.profiles ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.members ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE public.organisations ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- 2. Create policies to allow public (guest) users to see the data for the landing page
-- This is necessary for the counts and charts to appear
DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Allow Public Read Profiles" ON public.profiles;
CREATE POLICY "Allow Public Read Profiles" ON public.profiles FOR SELECT USING (true);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Allow Public Read Members" ON public.members;
CREATE POLICY "Allow Public Read Members" ON public.members FOR SELECT USING (true);

DROP POLICY IF EXISTS "Allow Public Read Organisations" ON public.organisations;
CREATE POLICY "Allow Public Read Organisations" ON public.organisations FOR SELECT USING (true);

-- 3. Standardize the 'Volunteer' role (Fix for the ERROR: 42883)
-- We cast the role to text using ::text before comparing
UPDATE public.profiles 
SET role = 'Volunteer' 
WHERE role::text ILIKE 'volunteer';
```

### 2. Application Update
I've updated the `LandingPage.tsx` to be more resilient. It now includes a "Case-Insensitive" check on the client side as well, ensuring that even if the database has minor naming variations, your counts will still be accurate.

