### Setup Instructions for Google Sheets

To complete the "automatic update" feature, follow these steps:

1.  Open your **Google Sheet**.
2.  Go to **Extensions** > **Apps Script**.
3.  Paste the following code into the script editor:

```javascript
function doPost(e) {
  var payload = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents);
  var sheetName = payload.sheetName;
  var data = payload.data;

  var ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  var sheet = ss.getSheetByName(sheetName) || ss.insertSheet(sheetName);

  // Create headers if empty
  if (sheet.getLastRow() === 0) {
    sheet.appendRow(Object.keys(data));
  }

  // Append the row
  var row = Object.keys(data).map(function(key) { return data[key]; });
  sheet.appendRow(row);

  return ContentService.createTextOutput("Success").setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.TEXT);
}
```

4.  Click **Deploy** > **New Deployment**.
5.  Select type **Web App**. Set access to **"Anyone"**.
6.  Copy the **Web App URL** provided.
7.  Paste this URL into the `WEB_APP_URL` variable inside `services/googleSheets.ts` in your app.

Now, every enrollment or authorization will automatically populate your Google Sheet in real-time.

