### 🚨 Action Required: Update your Google Apps Script
For the code above to work, your Google Apps Script (where you got that URL from) **must** look like this. Please copy-paste this into your Google Script editor and **Deploy > New Deployment** as "Anyone":

```javascript
function doPost(e) {
  try {
    // Parse the incoming JSON text
    var contents = JSON.parse(e.postData.contents);
    var sheetName = contents.sheetName;
    var data = contents.data;

    var ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
    var sheet = ss.getSheetByName(sheetName);

    // Create sheet if it doesn't exist
    if (!sheet) {
      sheet = ss.insertSheet(sheetName);
      // Create headers based on keys
      var headers = Object.keys(data);
      sheet.appendRow(headers);
      sheet.getRange(1, 1, 1, headers.length).setFontWeight("bold").setBackground("#f3f3f3");
    }

    // Map data to columns based on headers
    var headers = sheet.getRange(1, 1, 1, sheet.getLastColumn()).getValues()[0];
    var rowData = headers.map(function(header) {
      return data[header] || "";
    });

    sheet.appendRow(rowData);

    return ContentService.createTextOutput("Success").setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.TEXT);
  } catch (err) {
    return ContentService.createTextOutput("Error: " + err.message).setMimeType(ContentService.MimeType.TEXT);
  }
}
```

**Why it likely wasn't updating:**
1.  **CORS:** Standard `application/json` requests fail on Google Apps Script because of a hidden "Preflight" check. My fix using `text/plain` skips this check.
2.  **Deployment:** If you updated the script code but didn't click **"New Deployment"**, the URL points to an old version of your code. Always create a **New Deployment** when you change script logic.

